Found during k99 (worker). Two gaps, both documented in spec §6.2: (1) a url cache extracted by an earlier version has no executable bits and is reused while the server answers 304, so its scripts stay non-executable until the archive changes; (2) scripts installed by an earlier version get their bit only when a sync runs, and check has no reason to start one, so they stay non-executable until a source moves or the user runs `skilletor sync`. Possible fix: a one-time invalidation, e.g. a format number in the render-inputs record (k76) that makes check see drift once, plus a url cache format marker. Done: after upgrading, the next check/sync gives existing installs their executable bits without a source change.

2026-09-27 03:06 Plan: reuse the two existing records. Gap 2 (check has no reason to sync): a format number hashed into the k76 render-inputs record, so the hash an earlier version recorded differs once and check names the scope in varsChanged; the sync it starts records the new hash, so it fires once. No git cache is touched: git checkouts always kept the bit, the sync renders from them. Gap 1 (url cache without bits reused on 304): a format line in the k82 version file (.skilletor-version); a cache without it has no known version, exactly the k82 path for caches of skilletor <= 0.3.0: unconditional GET, re-extraction with bits, an offline fallback labelled 'unknown' (so check keeps counting the url source until a download succeeds). Tests first.

